meta {
  name: CreateMalformedJson
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/leverancier
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:text {
﻿{"levnr": 999999, "naam": "irrelevant"}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
  res.body.error.code: eq 400
}

docs {
  Regression test for a bug fixed in LeverancierHandler (and, identically,
  every other write-capable WebHandler - Artikel/Bon/Factuur/Klant/
  Lakproductie/Offerte): a malformed JSON body - here a leading UTF-8
  byte-order-mark (BOM) before the "{" - used to make the framework's own
  lazy request-body-to-JsonObject parse throw a plain (non-AppError) ABL
  error that HandlePost only ever caught as Progress.Lang.AppError, so it
  escaped uncaught into PASOE's generic error handler and came back as a
  raw 500 (HTML, or a JSON envelope with empty exception fields) instead
  of a documented error response. Must now return a clean 400
  {"error": {"message": "Malformed JSON request body: ...", "code": 400}}.
  Standalone request - no setup/cleanup needed (the body never reaches
  LeverancierBE).
}